From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 05:47:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 193/206] fix: near cascade under-injection, projector/area
 lights, cost overhaul

- Near cascade lost its GI with r_LPVCascadeScale > 1: the injection
  weight (gridSize/sampleCount)^2 silently assumed RSM span == volume
  span; with the RSM sized to the far cascade every surfel represents
  scale^2 more area and the near cascade was under-injected by 16x at
  scale 4. The weight now uses the MEASURED RSM texel size against the
  cascade cell size (also reused for the GV blocking potential).
- Local light injection handles projectors (emission gated to the
  frustum cone around the light X axis, soft edge) and area lights
  (hemisphere in front of the plane, radius extended by the area size).
- Cost overhaul (reported as more expensive than SVOGI): the RSM was
  re-rendered every frame (600+ casters, like an extra shadow cascade)
  and every crossed cell re-ran the full relight chain while moving.
  Now the RSM shadow pass only exists on the frames the LPV will
  relight on (CShadowMapStage asks WantsRsmRender(), same predicate as
  the relight gate; the stage injects from its own persistent depth
  target since the shadow prep stomps frustum.pDepthTex with the far
  plane on dropped frames), cell crossings no longer trigger relights
  (the frozen grid stays anchored and the heartbeat catches up; only a
  teleport sized jump forces one), and the far cascade runs half the
  propagation iterations (its cells are 4x larger). Static camera cost
  is now near zero, moving cost ~1/r_LPVUpdateInterval of before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
